en.fuller:
πατήρ, πατρός, -τρί, τέρα, [in LXX chiefly and very frequently for אָב ;]
a father;
__1. prop.,
__(a) of the male parent: Mat.2:22, Luk.1:17, Jhn.4:53; anarth., Heb.12:7 (M, Pr., 82 f.); pl., of both parents (cl.), Heb.11:23; οἱ π. τ. σαρκός, Heb.12:9;
__(b) of a forefather or ancestor (in cl. usually in pl.; Hom., al.): Mat.3:9, Luk.1:73, Jhn.8:39, al.; pl., Mat.23:30, 32 Luk.6:23, 26 Jhn.4:20, 1Co.10:1, al.
__2. Metaphorical,
__(a) of an author, originator, or archetype (= αἴτιος, ἀρχηγός, etc.; Pind., Plat., al.): Jhn.8:41-44, Rom.4:11, 12 16.
__(b) as a title of respect or honour, used of seniors, teachers and others in a position of responsible authority (Jdg.17:10, 2Ki.2:12, Pro.1:8, al.): Mat.23:9 Act.7:2 22:1, 1Jn.2:13.
__3. Of God (as in cl. of Zeus) as Father;
__(a) of created things: τ. φώτων, Jas.1:17;
__(b) of all sentient beings: Eph.3:14, 15 Heb.12:9;
__(with) of men, esp. those in covenant relation with Him (freq in OT and later Jewish lit.; see Dalman, Words, 184ff.): Mat.6:4, Luk.6:36, Jhn.4:21, Jas.3:9, al.; ὁ π. ὁ ἐν (τ.) οὐρανοῖς, Mat.5:16, Mrk.11:25; ὁ π. ὁ οὐράνιος, Mat.6:14 15:13; esp. in the Epp., of Christians: Rom.8:15, 2Co.6:18, Gal.4:6, Eph.2:18 4:6, 1Jn.2:1; with genitive qual., τ. οἰκτιρμῶν, 2Co.1:3; τ. δοξῆς, Eph.1:17;
__(d) of Christ (Dalman, Words, 190 ff.);
__(α) by our Lord himself: ὁ π., Mat.11:25-27, Luk.10:2, 22 Jhn.5:20-23, al.; ὁ π. μου, Mat.11:27, al.; ὁ ἐν τ. οὐρανοῖς, Mat.7:11, al.; ὁ οὐράνιος, Mat.15:13; vocat., Jhn.11:41 12:27, 28 17:1, 5, 11, 20, 25 (cf. Abbott, JG., 96 f.);
__(β) by Apostles: Jhn.1:14 (anarth.; see M, Pr., l.with), Rom.15:6, 2Co.1:3 11:31, Eph.1:3, Col.1:3, Heb.1:5, 1Pe.1:3, Rev.1:6 (cf. Westc., Epp. Jo., 27-34).
(AS)

he.fuller:
πατήρ, πατρός, -τρί, τέρα, [בשבעים בעיקר and very לעיתים קרובות for אָב ;]
a father;
1. בעיקרו,
(a) of the male parent: מתי.2:22, לוקס.1:17, יוחנן.4:53; anarth., עב.12:7 (M, Pr., 82 f.); pl., of both parents (קלאסית), עב.11:23; οἱ π. τ. σαρκός, עב.12:9;
(b) of a forefather or ancestor (בקלאסית usually in pl.; Hom., ועוד): מתי.3:9, לוקס.1:73, יוחנן.8:39, ועוד; pl., מתי.23:30, 32 לוקס.6:23, 26 יוחנן.4:20, 1קור.10:1, ועוד
2. Metaphorical,
(a) of an author, originator, or archetype (= αἴτιος, ἀρχηγός, ועוד; Pind., Plat., ועוד): יוחנן.8:41-44, רומים.4:11, 12 16.
(b) as a title of respect or honour, used of seniors, teachers and others in a position of responsible authority (שופ.17:10, 2מל.2:12, מש.1:8, ועוד): מתי.23:9 מע״ש.7:2 22:1, 1יוח.2:13.
3. Of God (as בקלאסית of Zeus) as Father;
(a) of created things: τ. φώτων, יעק.1:17;
(b) of all sentient beings: אפ.3:14, 15 עב.12:9;
(with) of men, במיוחד those in covenant relation with Him (freq in תנ״ך and later Jewish כפשוטו; see Dalman, Words, 184ff.): מתי.6:4, לוקס.6:36, יוחנן.4:21, יעק.3:9, ועוד; ὁ π. ὁ ἐν (τ.) οὐρανοῖς, מתי.5:16, מרקוס.11:25; ὁ π. ὁ οὐράνιος, מתי.6:14 15:13; במיוחד in the Epp., of Christians: רומים.8:15, 2קור.6:18, גל.4:6, אפ.2:18 4:6, 1יוח.2:1; עם יחס׳ qual., τ. οἰκτιρμῶν, 2קור.1:3; τ. δοξῆς, אפ.1:17;
(d) of משיח (Dalman, Words, 190 ff.);
(α) by our Lord himself: ὁ π., מתי.11:25-27, לוקס.10:2, 22 יוחנן.5:20-23, ועוד; ὁ π. μου, מתי.11:27, ועוד; ὁ ἐν τ. οὐρανοῖς, מתי.7:11, ועוד; ὁ οὐράνιος, מתי.15:13; vocat., יוחנן.11:41 12:27, 28 17:1, 5, 11, 20, 25 (השוו Abbott, JG., 96 f.);
(β) by Apostles: יוחנן.1:14 (anarth.; see M, Pr., l.with), רומים.15:6, 2קור.1:3 11:31, אפ.1:3, קל.1:3, עב.1:5, 1פ.1:3, התג.1:6 (השוו Westc., Epp. Jo., 27-34).
(AS)

en.fuller:
πειράζω poët. and late prose form of πειράω, which see,
[in LXX for נָסָה pi. ;]
__1. to make proof of (Hom.).
__2. to try, attempt (Luc., Polyb., with inf. (see M, Pr., 205; B1., § 69, 4), Act.9:26 16:7 24:6.
__3. In LXX and NT, like Heb. נָסָה, with accusative of person(s), to test, try, prove;
__(a) in a good sense : Jhn.6:6, 2Co.13:5, Heb.11:17, Rev.2:2; esp. of trials and af6ictions sent or permitted by God (Gen.22:1, Exo.20:20, Wis.3:5, al.), 1Co.10:13, Heb.2:18 4:15 11:17, 37, Rev.3:10;
__(b) in a bad sense (Apoll. Rhod., 3, 10): of the attempts made to ensnare Jesus in his speech, Mat.16:1 19:3 22:18, 35 Mrk.8:11 10:2 12:15, Luk.11:16, Jhn.8:6; of temptation to sin, to tempt, Jas.1:13-14 (see Hort, in l), Gal.6:1, Rev.2:10; esp. of temptations of the devil, Mat.4:1, 3 Mrk.1:13, Luk.4:2, 1Co.7:5, 1Th.3:5; ὁ πειράζων, the tempter, Mat.4:3, 1Th.3:5;
__(with) in bad sense also (Exo.17:2, 7, Num.14:22, al.), of distrustful testing, trying or challenging of God: Act.15:10, 1Co.10:9 (WH, mg., ἐξεπείρασαν), Heb.3:9; τ. πνεῦμα Κυρίου, Act.5:9 (of. ἐκ-πειράζω).†
SYN.: δοκιμάζω, q.v (AS)

he.fuller:
πειράζω poët. and late prose form of πειράω, ר׳ ערך,
[בשבעים for נָסָה פיעל ;]
1. to make proof of (Hom.).
2. to try, attempt (Luc., Polyb., עם מקור (see M, Pr., 205; B1., § 69, 4), מע״ש.9:26 16:7 24:6.
3. בשבעים and ברה״ח, like עב׳ נָסָה, עם ישי׳ של אדם, to test, try, prove;
(a) in a good sense : יוחנן.6:6, 2קור.13:5, עב.11:17, התג.2:2; במיוחד of trials and af6ictions sent or permitted by God (בר.22:1, שמ.20:20, חכמ.3:5, ועוד), 1קור.10:13, עב.2:18 4:15 11:17, 37, התג.3:10;
(b) in a bad sense (Apoll. Rhod., 3, 10): of the attempts made to ensnare Jesus in his speech, מתי.16:1 19:3 22:18, 35 מרקוס.8:11 10:2 12:15, לוקס.11:16, יוחנן.8:6; of temptation to sin, to tempt, יעק.1:13-14 (ר׳ Hort, in l), גל.6:1, התג.2:10; במיוחד of temptations of the devil, מתי.4:1, 3 Mrk.1:13, לוקס.4:2, 1קור.7:5, 1תס.3:5; ὁ πειράζων, the tempter, מתי.4:3, 1תס.3:5;
(with) in bad sense also (שמ.17:2, 7, במ.14:22, ועוד), of distrustful testing, trying or challenging of God: מע״ש.15:10, 1קור.10:9 (WH, mg., ἐξεπείρασαν), עב.3:9; τ. πνεῦμα Κυρίου, מע״ש.5:9 (of. ἐκ-πειράζω).†
נרדף: δοκιμάζω, q.v (AS)

